---
id: roasted-sweet-potatoes-feta
title: Roasted Sweet Potatoes with Feta
category: modular_carb

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 255

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Set the #oven to convection 200°C (400°F) and let it preheat fully, about 10 to 15 minutes.

Scrub @sweet-potatoes{1} well under running water and leave the skin on; it crisps up and holds a good share of the fibre. Trim the ends and cut into 2.5 cm (1-inch) cubes, then pat them dry with a towel so they roast instead of steam.

In a large bowl, toss the cubes with @avocado-oil{1%tsp} until lightly coated, then with @smoked-paprika{1/2%tsp}, @garlic-powder{1/4%tsp}, @kosher-salt{1/4%tsp}, and @black-pepper{1/8%tsp}.

Spread the cubes in a single layer on the mesh basket of the #crisper-tray, not touching, so the air can reach every side. Roast on the middle rack for ~roast{22%minute}, tossing them once halfway, until a fork slides in easily and the edges are browned. Crumble @greek-feta{30%g} evenly over the cubes and roast for ~feta{3%minute} more, until the feta softens and turns golden at the edges.

Divide between 2 meal prep containers (about 115 g each) and let cool before sealing. Reheat in the #microwave for about a minute (they soften), or in a hot #skillet for 3 to 4 minutes to bring back some crispness.
